# The NEGATIVE control for .github/scripts/assert_provider_linked.sh (#46).
#
# A REAL, UNMODIFIED, previously-published build of this fork that genuinely has
# no KMS provider linked into it. The gate must go RED on this file, and until
# it has been watched do so its green on a healthy artifact says nothing.
#
# Why a published asset rather than a fixture manufactured on the spot: the
# obvious plant is to take the good artifact and delete the provider records
# with `objcopy --strip-symbols`. That is CIRCULAR - it manufactures the fixture
# by deleting exactly the table the gate reads, so the refusal is guaranteed by
# construction and proves nothing about the gate. It is also not even a
# provider-less binary: objcopy rewrites .symtab and leaves .dynsym alone, so
# the "stripped" library still exports the provider and would still register
# the factory at load. Measured on the artifact of run 32756499818:
#     .dynsym  21 GLOBAL DEF + 7 WEAK DEF provider symbols
#     .symtab  the same 28, plus 20 LOCAL DEF
# Stripping .symtab removes 48 records and changes nothing about what the
# library does.
#
# So the control is this instead: bytes nobody here made, from the release
# ducklake#33 was filed about. sha256 is pinned so the control cannot silently
# become a different file - a negative control that quietly changed identity is
# a negative control nobody is testing.
#
#   $ gh release download v0.2.0-rc.2 -R sigil-enterprises/ducklake \
#       --pattern ducklake.duckdb_extension
#   $ file ducklake.duckdb_extension
#   PE32+ executable (DLL) (console) x86-64, for MS Windows
#   $ .github/scripts/assert_provider_linked.sh --expect present ducklake.duckdb_extension
#       symbols     250316
#       anchor(DuckLakeCatalog) 505
#       provider    0
#   exit 1
#
# 250316 symbols and 505 anchor sightings are what make the 0 mean something:
# the symbol table is demonstrably real and demonstrably a DuckLake one, so the
# zero is an absent provider and not a misaimed tool.
CONTROL_TAG=v0.2.0-rc.2
CONTROL_ASSET=ducklake.duckdb_extension
CONTROL_SHA256=4c68ec6d0ed6f85b8d3eb1893aaeb4220b6a701863553c61afbf259b72bda315
